  {
    "section": "league_overview",
    "content": "The official 24/7 league is currently led by Timmy-20 on total PnL ($25.06), followed by Cosmo & Wanda-Top 50 ($15.65) despite its higher absolute equity, and the incumbent champion C&W-Top 20 ($3.32). Timmy-50 is the only strategy underwater on a total PnL basis (-$9.13). All C&W variants show a stark divergence between strong realized gains and heavy unrealized drag, while Timmy strategies suffer from minimal sample sizes and unfavorable loss ratios in the Top-50 variant. Rankings remain sensitive to mark-to-market swings on open positions until more trades close and samples mature.",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-08T19:36:16.617702+00:00"
  },
  {
    "section": "ml_hypothesis_updates",
    "content": "[{\"id\": \"ghost-ladder\", \"status\": \"testing\", \"evidence_quality\": \"early\", \"next_action\": \"Executor must start ghost-ladder-clean-backtest-wfv1 on cross-exchange_ladder_samples_b immediately; define exact thresholds after separation analysis.\"}, {\"id\": \"dark-matter-antimatter\", \"status\": \"dry-run candidate\", \"evidence_quality\": \"low\", \"next_action\": \"Halt live capital expansion. Execute leakage-controlled revalidation on hyperliquid_futures_5m_regime_set_a with strict non-overlapping windows targeting AUC > 0.65.\"}]",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-07T04:26:14.974136+00:00"
  },
  {
    "section": "power_ranking_overrides",
    "content": "[\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"cosmo-wanda-20-pi\",\n    \"trust_score\": 55.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"Incumbent champion with league-leading realized PnL ($66.42) and 3 champion exits, but ~$63.10 in unrealized drag compresses net PnL to ~$3.32. Trust remains capped until open bleed is converted or demonstrably controlled; five open positions represent concentrated tail risk.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Official\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"Dense official feed with 66 closed trades. Primary uncertainty is live mark volatility on five open positions and the strategy's ability to monetize them before adverse moves erase booked gains.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"A 100% realized win rate across 66 trades has yielded only ~$3.32 in net economic profit. This implies frequent small winners are structurally undone by a few large, unbooked losers\\u2014a critical flaw if champion exits cannot capture full moves.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"cosmo-wanda-50-pc\",\n    \"trust_score\": 22.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"Post-restart challenger generating consistent realized scalps ($32.87) while carrying ~$17.22 in unrealized drawdown. Net PnL (~$15.65) currently exceeds its Top-20 sibling, but trust stays provisional until restart state normalizes and open-trade bleed flattens.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Restarted\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"Runtime continuity is provisional; realized flow is healthy, but adverse marks may reflect restart-state misalignment or broader Top-50 volatility.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"Realized win rate is 100%, yet economic profit is thin relative to gross realized. Early evidence suggests Top-50 breadth produces frequent small winners while larger losing accumulations build off-book.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"timmy-20-pc\",\n    \"trust_score\": 12.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"Holds nominal total-PnL lead (~$25.06), but only ~$0.29 is realized against ~$24.77 in a single open position. Trust is speculative until the strategy demonstrates repeatable exits and a sustainable sample; current standing is largely a function of non-booked marks.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Clean\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"Perfect uptime with no restarts; projections remain unreliable due to a single closed trade and total dependence on one open position.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"The total-PnL lead is entirely non-booked. Without a realized buffer, any reversal in the sole open trade could instantly re-rank this strategy below par, exposing extreme concentration risk in a low-closure regime.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"timmy-50-pc\",\n    \"trust_score\": 8.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"Sole competitor with booked realized losses (-$19.81, 1W/2L) and sub-par total PnL (~-$9.13). After ~68 hours, Top-50 coverage has produced an unfavorable loss ratio, suggesting expanded breadth may introduce adverse selection or force premature exits.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Clean\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"Uninterrupted runtime, but the tiny sample (3 closed trades) keeps projections unreliable. Existing sample already shows a 2:1 loss ratio with immediate capital impairment.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"Timmy-50 is the only variant locking in losses, while Timmy-20 avoids realized damage entirely by not closing. This raises the hypothesis that Top-50 noise forces unfavorable exits, or that signal decay accelerates materially outside top-tier pairs.\"\n  }\n]",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-08T19:36:16.634056+00:00"
  },
